        "original_id": "c7adad80-f17e-5c2c-afa2-6e6fe840bd18",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Clare, Jonathan Bate, Matthew Allen\n- Organizations: University of Oxford, Worcester College Oxford, Warwick Business School\n- Places: High Beach\n- Works: The Quickening Maze\n- Concepts: English literature, labouring-class poetry, mental asylum\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1830s and 1840s, Matthew Allen ran a mental asylum at High Beach.\n- In the late 1830s and 1840s, John Clare was admitted to Matthew Allen's mental asylum at High Beach.\n- The Quickening Maze is based on the historical backdrop of the mental asylum run by Matthew Allen at High Beach in the late 1830s and 1840s.\n- Jonathan Bate stated that John Clare was \"the greatest labouring-class poet that England has ever produced.\"\n- Jonathan Bate is Professor of English Literature at the University of Oxford, Provost of Worcester College, Oxford, and Honorary Fellow of Creativity at Warwick Business School.",
